==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/zuːm/}}, {{enPR|zo͞om}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-zoom.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːm|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{unc|en}}. The verb was attested in 1892, noun in 1918 and interjection in 1942. Apparently related to {{cog|sco|soom|t=to buzz, hum}}, dialectal English and {{m+|sco|soom}}, {{m|en|swoom}}, {{m|sco|sweem|t=to spin or twirl at high speed}}. Compare also dialectal {{m+|en|sweem|t=to swoon, become dizzy or faint}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A humming [[noise]] from something moving very fast.
#: {{ux|en|the '''zoom''' of traffic}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A quick [[ascent]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A big [[increase]].
# An [[augmentation]] of a [[view]], by varying the [[focal length]] of a [[lens]], or digitally.
#: {{ux|en|What's the '''zoom''' like on your camera?}}

